The attached image illustrates that Nano-11, when injected intramuscularly with ovalbumin, induces a transient inflammatory response at the injection site and is taken up by various recruited immune cells. Panel A shows an influx of immune cells, predominantly Mac-2+ macrophages and Ly6C+ monocytes peaking around Day 2, with neutrophils and eosinophils appearing in smaller numbers, all subsiding by Day 21. Panel B's confocal images confirm Nano-11 (red) uptake by MHCII+ cells, Ly6C+ monocytes, and Mac-2+ macrophages (green) at early time points, demonstrating its interaction with antigen-presenting cells at the injection site.